# Text files are stored and checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true otherwise turns every text file
# into CRLF, and two things break: the Postgres image cannot run
# docker/postgres-init/01-roles.sh ("cannot execute: required file not
# found", the shell looks for "bash\r"), and `pnpm format:check` flags every
# file because Prettier expects LF. Git still detects binaries (images,
# fonts) on its own and leaves them alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
